  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(\\land)$ and \"or\" $(\\lor)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A \\land B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is false, $Q$ is false, and $R$ is false. Therefore, $P \\lor Q$ is false, and the result is false:\n\\begin{align*}\n(P \\lor Q)\\lor R \n&\\equiv \\overbrace{(\\textrm{false} \\lor \\textrm{false})}^{\\textrm{false}} \\lor \\text{false} \\\\[5pt]\n&\\equiv \\textrm{false} \\lor \\textrm{false} \\\\[3pt]\n&\\equiv \\textrm{false}\n\\end{align*}",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
